# Read by both Cloudflare Pages and Netlify, so the same headers apply
# wherever the client's account ends up being. Netlify also has these in
# netlify.toml; duplicated deliberately, because whichever host is chosen has
# to work on its own.
#
# Deliberately no Content-Security-Policy yet. A CSP has to name the form
# endpoint and the analytics host, and the analytics provider is not chosen
# (MISSING-ASSETS.md 5). A CSP written against a guess would block the
# enquiry POST, which is the one failure this codebase must never have
# (rule 2.4). It is a launch task, listed in the README.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

# Fingerprinted by Astro, so these can never go stale.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
